> Any tips?  I guess I should go for a few scrolls of charging with the
> wand first, yeah?  But beyond that?

First the scrolls of charging, as you said. Unless you've seen a
scroll of charging before, in which case get a magic marker and write
another one (be sure it's blessed).

Even if you wish for the scrolls, get a magic marker anyway. Enchant
armor and enchant weapon are both nice to have in abundance, as is
identify.  And genocide. Also gold detection...suffice to say, if you
wished for 2 scrolls of charging, the second one should be used on
marker.

Then speed boots. (blessed +2 rustproof)

If you found a shield of reflection anywhere (check the statues in
Medusa's isle if you haven't already), I'd recommend swapping the
amulet for lifesaving.  If not, you'll have to decide whether you're
willing to spend two wishes to get a shield of reflection AND an
amulet of life saving.

You'll also need some source of levitation for Air, and a ring
of conflict is highly recommended.  But both are nonessential for
Gehennom, so I'd suggest you save the wishes and see if they turn up.
(Conflict should be used with caution since you've got that worm.)
Same for a wand of death.  You'll want at least one fully charged one
during the endgame, but don't spend the wish just yet.

If you can, save a non-wrest wish for a cockatrice corpse on Astral,
but if you need to use them all, cursed genocide on Water will
probably leave a corpse.  And a Valkyrie with a pet worm has a good
chance of making it through Astral even without one.


